    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situated in the heart of the ever-popular Frankfield area, 61 Frankfield, Douglas, Cork is a superb four bedroom detached bungalow offering an exceptional opportunity to acquire a home in one of Cork's most established and sought-after residential locations. Properties in this mature neighbourhood seldom come to the market, making this a truly special offering.\r\nThe property is approached through a gated entrance, providing excellent privacy and ample off-street parking.  A generous area to the side of the house offers space for an additional vehicle or presents excellent potential to extend the property subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\nTo the rear lies a beautifully landscaped south facing private garden, a real highlight of the home. Designed to maximise sunshine throughout the day, it features a greenhouse, garden shed and an abundance of mature planting, creating the perfect setting for gardening enthusiasts, outdoor entertaining or simply relaxing in peaceful surroundings.\r\nInternally, the accommodation is bright and well laid out comprising a welcoming entrance hallway, spacious living room, kitchen/dining room, four generous bedrooms including a main bedroom with en suite, and a family bathroom.  There is also a large attic space with the potential for conversion into further living accommodation.\r\nCombining spacious accommodation, a magnificent garden and outstanding potential, 61 Frankfield is a rare opportunity to secure a forever home in one of Douglas's most desirable residential settings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch\r\nSliding patio door, floor tiles.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway\r\nTeak front door to hallway, mix of floor tiles and carpet floor covering, 3 centre lights, Stira stairs to semi floored attic for storage purposes.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\n14’5 X 12’1\r\nCarpet floor covering, gas fire, radiator, centre light, 2 windows, curtain and curtain pole facing the front of the property.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room\r\n19’10 X 14’3\r\nTerracotta floor tiles, shaker style fitted kitchen at floor and eye level, tiled splash back, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher, ceramic hob with stainless steel extractor over, electric stainless steel oven, recessed lighting, dual aspect windows facing the front and side of the property with roman window blinds, door exiting to the side of the property, 2 radiators.\r\n \r\nBedroom One\r\n12’4 X 10’2\r\nSemi-solid walnut floor covering, radiator, centre light, built in wardrobes, two windows with roman window blinds.\r\n\r\nEnsuite\r\n7’4 X 3’4\r\nWC, WHB, pump shower, floor tiles, wall tiles, tiled shower area, xpelair, centre light, window with frosted glass facing side of property.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two\r\n11’3 X 11’10\r\nLaminate oak effect wood floor covering, radiator, centre light, 2 windows with curtain and curtain rail facing rear of property.\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom Three\r\n8’5 X 8’12\r\nLaminate oak effect wood floor covering, radiator, centre light, window with curtain and curtain rail facing rear of property.\r\n\r\nBedroom Four\r\n10’3 X 6’3\r\nCarpet floor covering, radiator, centre light, window with curtain and curtain rail facing side of property.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\n10’10 X 5’01\r\nWC, WHB, bath with electric shower and shower curtain over, floor and wall tiles, radiator, centre light, xpelair, window with frosted glass facing side of property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Superb four bedroom detached bungalow.\r\nLarge private and matured south facing rear garden.\r\nGated entrance with off street parking.\r\nRoom to extend to side subject to planning permission.\r\nExcellent condition throughout.\r\nHighly desirable location where properties seldom come to market."
      },
      {
